        "passages": [
          {
            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Echium nervosum is a species of flowering plants of the family Boraginaceae. It is endemic to Madeira. The specific name nervosum is from Latin and means \"veined\"."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "Description\nIt is a compact woody shrub, average height {{convert|100|cm}}, maximum height {{convert|150|cm}}. The leaves are narrow, densely haired and silver green. Its flowers are pale blue to pale bluish rose and sit in an egg-shaped inflorescence."
          }
        ]
      }
